# Denylist terms — template
#
# Copy this file to `.denylist.local` and replace the placeholders with the actual
# terms you need to keep out of this repository: names of people, employers,
# institutions, products, and anything else that identifies someone.
#
#     cp .denylist.local.example .denylist.local
#
# `.denylist.local` is gitignored and MUST STAY THAT WAY. It is the one file in this
# repo that contains the information the project exists to protect. A committed list of
# the names we are hiding would publish exactly what the check prevents, and hashing
# them is not a fix — proper nouns are short and fall to a dictionary attack.
#
# Consequence, stated plainly: CI cannot see `.denylist.local`, so the term check runs
# only on machines that have one. CI enforces the structural patterns (emails, phone
# numbers) and nothing else. See the header of scripts/check-denylist.mjs.
#
# Format: one term per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# Matching is case-insensitive and word-boundary aware, so `Ackerman` catches
# `ackerman` and `Ackerman's` but not `Ackermanized`. Multi-word entries are fine.

# --- people (replace these placeholders) ---
PLACEHOLDER_GIVEN_NAME
PLACEHOLDER_SURNAME
PLACEHOLDER_FULL_NAME

# --- employer, manufacturer, product ---
PLACEHOLDER_EMPLOYER
PLACEHOLDER_PRODUCT

# --- institutions and sites ---
PLACEHOLDER_HOSPITAL
PLACEHOLDER_CITY
